WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.026 --> 00:00:02.693
(ominous music)

00:00:24.775 --> 00:00:26.775
(thump)

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:36.430
- This is your new home.

00:00:40.869 --> 00:00:41.702
- Home.

00:00:43.329 --> 00:00:46.149
(upbeat music)

00:00:46.149 --> 00:00:48.981
♪ Uptown got it's hustlers ♪

00:00:48.981 --> 00:00:51.910
♪ The bowery got it's bums ♪

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:53.128
♪ 42nd street got big Jim walker ♪

00:00:53.128 --> 00:00:55.304
- All right, let's get to work.

00:00:55.304 --> 00:00:57.491
♪ He's a pool shooting son of a gun ♪

00:00:57.491 --> 00:00:59.539
♪ Yeah, he big and dumb
as a man can come ♪

00:00:59.539 --> 00:01:00.715
(coughing)

00:01:00.715 --> 00:01:04.864
♪ But he stronger than a country hoss ♪

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:07.123
(bong)
- Oh, Jesus.

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:09.620
- [Eleven] Ghost.

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:11.550
- Yeah, I see that.

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:12.383
- [Eleven] Halloween.

00:01:12.383 --> 00:01:16.637
- Sure is but right now
it's breakfast, okay.

00:01:16.637 --> 00:01:20.705
- [Eleven] Trick or treat.

00:01:20.705 --> 00:01:22.659
- You wanna go trick or treating?

00:01:22.659 --> 00:01:25.409
(dramatic music)

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:27.620
You know the rules.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:28.453
- [Eleven] Yes.

00:01:28.453 --> 00:01:29.286
- Yes, so you know the answer.

00:01:29.286 --> 00:01:30.527
- [Eleven] No but I don't,
they wouldn't see me.

00:01:30.527 --> 00:01:34.320
- Hey, I don't care, I
don't care all right.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:37.440
You go out there, ghost
or not, it's a risk.

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:40.640
We don't take risks, all right.

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:41.530
They're stupid

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:43.490
and

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:45.123
- [Eleven] We're not stupid.

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:48.023
- Exactly.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.800
I do wish she lived long enough for me

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:52.870
to remember calling her mother

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:54.790
and it would be so sweet to say mother.

00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:56.433
- Do I have mother?

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:00.070
- Yeah, of course you have a mother.

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:01.963
You couldn't really be born without one.

00:02:03.705 --> 00:02:04.955
- Where is she?

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:10.660
- She's not around anymore.

00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:13.663
- Gone?

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:16.023
- Yeah.

00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:23.080
I'm sorry about that kid.

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:26.170
You gonna see them soon.

00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:27.450
And not just in that head of yours,

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:30.083
you gonna see them in real life.

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:33.720
I feel like I'm making
progress with these people.

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:36.980
- Friends don't lie.

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:38.050
- What?

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:40.490
- You say soon on day 21,

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:43.970
you say soon on day 205,

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:46.923
you now say soon on day 326.

00:02:46.923 --> 00:02:49.010
- What is this, you like
counting the days now

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:50.389
like you're some kind of prisoner?

00:02:50.389 --> 00:02:52.489
- When is soon?

00:02:52.489 --> 00:02:56.870
- Soon is when it's not dangerous anymore.

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:57.703
- When?

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:02.153
- I don't know.

00:03:02.153 --> 00:03:03.073
- On day 500?

00:03:03.073 --> 00:03:03.906
- I don't know.

00:03:03.906 --> 00:03:04.739
- On day 600?

00:03:04.739 --> 00:03:05.572
- I don't know.

00:03:05.572 --> 00:03:07.406
- Day 700, on day 800.

00:03:07.406 --> 00:03:09.362
I need to see him!
- Jesus!

00:03:09.362 --> 00:03:10.718
I said I--
(shatters)

00:03:10.718 --> 00:03:11.801
Ah shit!
Shit.

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:16.733
- Friends don't lie.

00:03:19.367 --> 00:03:20.200
(whoosh)

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.033
(thump)

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:22.923
You promised.

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:26.733
I go and I never leave.

00:03:28.234 --> 00:03:29.877
Nothing ever happens.

00:03:29.877 --> 00:03:33.294
- Yeah nothing happens and you stay safe.

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:37.200
- You lie.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:39.470
- I don't lie, I protect

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:41.320
and I feed and I teach.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:45.400
And all I ask of you is that
you follow three simple rules.

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:47.873
Three rules and you know one,

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:50.873
you can't even do that.

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:55.100
- I hate you.

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:57.280
- Yeah well, I'm not too
crazy about you either.

00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:58.113
You know why?

00:03:58.113 --> 00:04:00.850
'Cause you're a brat, you
know what that word means?

00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:02.980
How about that be your
word for the day, huh?

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:04.600
Brat, why don't we look it up?

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:06.841
B-R-A-T, brat.

00:04:06.841 --> 00:04:08.924
(swoosh)

00:04:10.355 --> 00:04:11.760
(whoosh)

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:14.915
Hey, what the hell is wrong with you?

00:04:14.915 --> 00:04:15.748
(whoosh)

00:04:15.748 --> 00:04:17.512
(grunts)

00:04:17.512 --> 00:04:19.130
Hey!

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:20.705
Hey!

00:04:20.705 --> 00:04:21.538
(whoosh)
(thump)

00:04:21.538 --> 00:04:22.679
Hey!
Hey!

00:04:22.679 --> 00:04:24.567
(whoosh)
(thump)

00:04:24.567 --> 00:04:26.410
Open this door!

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:28.470
Open the dam door!

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:30.459
You wanna go out in the world,

00:04:30.459 --> 00:04:31.875
you better grow up.

00:04:31.875 --> 00:04:33.412
Grow the hell up!

00:04:33.412 --> 00:04:34.839
(screams)

00:04:34.839 --> 00:04:37.089
(shatters)

00:04:38.296 --> 00:04:40.463
(jingles)

00:04:42.245 --> 00:04:44.162
(sobs)

00:04:49.025 --> 00:04:52.373
So what, we're not just
gonna talk about it, huh?

00:04:52.373 --> 00:04:53.530
- About what?

00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:54.680
- Oh, I don't know.

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:56.021
I'm just curious you know

00:04:56.021 --> 00:04:58.721
why all of a sudden you look
like some kinda MTV punk.

00:04:59.883 --> 00:05:01.966
I should have been there.

00:05:04.155 --> 00:05:07.484
I should never have lied
to you about your mom.

00:05:07.484 --> 00:05:10.173
Or about when you can leave.

00:05:10.173 --> 00:05:14.170
A lot of things I shouldn't have done.

00:05:14.170 --> 00:05:15.003
I'm so sorry

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:17.113
for every thing.

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:21.386
I can be so,

00:05:23.230 --> 00:05:24.170
so,

00:05:24.170 --> 00:05:25.474
- Stupid.

00:05:25.474 --> 00:05:27.622
(laughs)
- Yeah.

00:05:27.622 --> 00:05:28.455
Stupid.

00:05:29.734 --> 00:05:31.317
Just really stupid.

00:05:37.715 --> 00:05:40.439
- I've been stupid too.

00:05:40.439 --> 00:05:42.772
- I guess we broke our rule.

00:05:44.459 --> 00:05:46.643
I don't hate it by the way

00:05:46.643 --> 00:05:47.476
this whole

00:05:49.441 --> 00:05:50.274
look.

00:05:52.416 --> 00:05:53.333
Kinda cool.

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:56.153
- Bitchen.

00:05:58.488 --> 00:05:59.571
- Okay, sure.

00:06:04.824 --> 00:06:05.657
Bitchen.

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:09.840
(freakish roars)

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:11.305
Ah, shit!

00:06:11.305 --> 00:06:13.638
(gun shots)

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:19.241
(clicks)

00:06:19.241 --> 00:06:20.668
(squealing)

00:06:20.668 --> 00:06:23.001
(gun shots)

00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:26.893
(whoosh)

00:06:32.298 --> 00:06:34.854
(grunts)

00:06:34.854 --> 00:06:37.278
(background chatter of TV)

00:06:37.278 --> 00:06:39.528
(creaking)

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:47.142
Hey!

00:06:47.142 --> 00:06:48.137
(whoosh)
(thump)

00:06:48.137 --> 00:06:48.970
Hey!

00:06:50.177 --> 00:06:51.780
Three inch minimum.

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:52.613
Leave the door open

00:06:52.613 --> 00:06:53.697
(thump)
three inches.

00:06:54.664 --> 00:06:56.970
(rattle)

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:58.020
El.
(thumps)

00:06:58.020 --> 00:06:59.003
Open this door,

00:06:59.949 --> 00:07:00.782
open the--

00:07:04.647 --> 00:07:06.098
- What's wrong?

00:07:06.098 --> 00:07:07.838
- No overcharge.

00:07:07.838 --> 00:07:10.600
- I know little kid, I know.

00:07:10.600 --> 00:07:11.743
- I can fight.

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:14.253
- Better than any of us.

00:07:15.460 --> 00:07:18.363
But right now, I need you safe.

00:07:20.480 --> 00:07:21.723
This thing is after you.

00:07:23.110 --> 00:07:24.193
It's not after me.

00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:28.140
Do you understand?

00:07:30.218 --> 00:07:31.051
Hey.

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:35.553
I need you to understand.

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:43.693
- It's the speech, Hopper
wrote for you and Mike.

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:46.100
- Speech?

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:49.013
- Yeah, you know the heart to heart.

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:53.213
He never talked to you did he?

00:07:58.371 --> 00:07:59.204
(rustling)

00:07:59.204 --> 00:08:00.037
- Can I read?

00:08:03.597 --> 00:08:05.847
(rustling)

00:08:12.633 --> 00:08:13.540
- [Hopper Voiceover]
Something I've been wanting

00:08:13.540 --> 00:08:15.203
to talk to you both about.

00:08:17.320 --> 00:08:19.610
I know this is a difficult conversation

00:08:19.610 --> 00:08:22.323
but I care about you both very much.

00:08:23.290 --> 00:08:25.780
And I know that you care
about each other very much

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:27.390
and that's why it's important that we set

00:08:27.390 --> 00:08:29.700
these boundaries moving forward

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:31.280
so we can build an environment

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:39.663
where we all feel comfortable,

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:45.310
trusted and open

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:49.943
to sharing our feelings.

00:08:55.646 --> 00:08:57.255
Feelings.

00:08:57.255 --> 00:08:59.338
(clicks)

00:09:02.491 --> 00:09:04.491
(thump)

00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:09.653
Feelings.

00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:12.743
Jesus.

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:15.450
The truth is

00:09:17.190 --> 00:09:19.360
for so long I've forgotten

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:20.423
what those even were.

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:27.040
I've been stuck in one place,
in a cave you might say.

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:28.433
A deep, dark cave.

00:09:29.592 --> 00:09:32.560
And then I left some
Eggo's out in the woods

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:34.240
and you came into my whole life

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:37.350
and for the first time

00:09:37.350 --> 00:09:38.793
in a long time,

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:43.153
I started to feel things again.

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:45.940
I started to feel happy

00:09:50.550 --> 00:09:53.170
but lately, I guess I've been feeling

00:09:55.140 --> 00:09:56.220
distant from you

00:09:57.930 --> 00:10:01.693
like you're going away
from me or something.

00:10:03.320 --> 00:10:05.313
I miss playing board games every night,

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:11.760
making triple-decker Eggo
extravaganzas at sunrise,

00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:14.260
watching Westerns together
before we dose off

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:17.980
but I know you're getting older.

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:20.243
Growing,

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:22.303
changing

00:10:24.090 --> 00:10:25.110
and I guess

00:10:26.300 --> 00:10:27.810
if I'm being really honest

00:10:29.110 --> 00:10:30.210
that's what scares me.

00:10:32.626 --> 00:10:34.080
I don't want things to change

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:41.070
so I think maybe that's why I came in here

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:43.993
to try to maybe stop that change,

00:10:46.070 --> 00:10:47.540
to turn back the clock

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:50.150
to make things go

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:51.783
back to how they were.

00:10:53.302 --> 00:10:55.802
(deep breath)

00:10:56.700 --> 00:10:58.103
But I know that's naive,

00:10:59.240 --> 00:11:02.710
it's just not how life works

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:04.493
it's moving,

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:08.053
always moving whether you like it or not.

00:11:10.090 --> 00:11:13.303
And yeah, sometimes it's painful,

00:11:14.670 --> 00:11:15.660
sometimes it's sad

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:21.303
and sometimes it's surprising,

00:11:23.130 --> 00:11:23.963
happy.

00:11:26.350 --> 00:11:27.200
So you know what,

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:30.033
keep on growing up kid,

00:11:31.060 --> 00:11:32.160
don't let me stop you.

00:11:33.510 --> 00:11:35.860
Make mistakes, learn from them

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:38.280
and when life hurts you

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:39.993
because it will,

00:11:41.080 --> 00:11:42.543
remember the hurt.

00:11:43.557 --> 00:11:46.063
The hurt is good,

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:49.260
it means you're out of that cave

00:11:51.680 --> 00:11:53.320
but please

00:11:54.170 --> 00:11:56.710
if you don't mind,

00:11:56.710 --> 00:11:59.203
for the sake of your poor old dad,

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:04.034
keep the door open three inches.

00:12:04.034 --> 00:12:06.117
(laughs)

00:12:07.022 --> 00:12:08.939
(sobs)

00:12:16.814 --> 00:12:20.049
♪ I won't be king ♪

00:12:20.049 --> 00:12:22.299
(knocking)

00:12:23.206 --> 00:12:24.456
- Are you okay?

00:12:27.681 --> 00:12:31.581
- Yeah.
(sobs)

00:12:32.986 --> 00:12:33.903
Time to go?

00:12:35.733 --> 00:12:36.566
- Yeah.

00:12:37.954 --> 00:12:40.186
- I'll be out in a minute.

00:12:40.186 --> 00:12:42.269
(sniffs)

00:12:43.349 --> 00:12:48.349
♪ Or we could be heroes ♪

00:12:48.977 --> 00:12:53.947
♪ Just for a day ♪

00:12:53.947 --> 00:12:58.947
♪ Or we can be us ♪

00:12:59.370 --> 00:13:02.287
♪ Just for one day ♪

